  "answer": "Requests treats HTTP header names case-insensitively. `Content-Type`, `content-type`, and other casing variants refer to the same header because request headers use a `CaseInsensitiveDict`. Therefore, `headers.pop(\"Content-Type\", None)` also removes a header originally supplied as `content-type`. The value is associated with one normalized case-insensitive key, while the most recently assigned spelling may be preserved for output.",
